    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(x)=x^2-2x-3$.",
      "worked": "For $x\\ge0$, the displayed graph is $y=f(x)$. Since $f$ is monic, write $f(x)=x^2+bx+c$. The labelled intercepts give $f(0)=-3$ and $f(3)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}c&=-3\\\\f(3)&=9+3b-3=0\\\\b&=-2\\\\f(x)&=x^2-2x-3\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
